# CRYPTARCH-108. The compose defaults now point outside the stack directory,
# but the README still has you generating a key with openssl in whatever
# directory you are standing in — and `git status` showing `cryptarch.key` as
# untracked is one `git add -A` away from publishing the AES-256 key that
# decrypts every backup blob and every stored managed-server admin DSN.
# Losing that key is documented as unrecoverable; leaking it was not.
/cryptarch.key

# Backups, if anyone points them here anyway. They are large, they are
# sealed data, and this directory is one `git clean -fdx` from gone.
/backups/
